-- title:
--   No level raising at r after localising at 𝔪
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero complete discrete valuation ring (a domain, complete for the maximal-ideal-adic topology) with finite residue field $k=\operatorname{ResidueField}\mathcal O$, and let $p$ be a prime with $p\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$. Let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$, that is a two-dimensional $k$-vector space $V$ together with a monoid homomorphism $\rho$ from $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ (the $\mathbb Q$-algebra automorphisms of $\operatorname{AlgebraicClosure}\mathbb Q$) to $\operatorname{End}_k V$ factoring through a finite level, and assume $\bar\rho$ is absolutely irreducible (its base change to $\overline k$ is irreducible). Let $S$ be a finite set of naturals with $p\in S$, and $N\ne 0$ with every prime divisor of $N$ in $S$. Let $r\ne 0$ be a prime with $r\notin S$, $r\nmid N$, such that for every valuation subring $P$ of $\operatorname{AlgebraicClosure}\mathbb Q$ with $r$ a non-unit of $P$ and every $\sigma$ lying in the decomposition subgroup of $P$ and acting on the residue field of $P$ by $x\mapsto x^r$, one has $\operatorname{tr}(\bar\rho(\sigma))^2\ne(r+1)^2$. Let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism to $k$ from the anemic weight-two Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) (the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the Hecke generators away from $S$), and assume that for every prime $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S$, every valuation subring over $\ell$ and every Frobenius $\sigma$ at $\ell$ in the above sense, $\operatorname{charpoly}(\bar\rho(\sigma))=X^2-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$. Assume [`CuspForm.AuxLevel.MidOpComm N r S 𝒪`](def/CuspForm_AuxLevelHeckeModuleMid.html#L14), i.e. the operators `midOp N r S 𝒪 g` for $g$ in `Gen N r S` commute pairwise, and let `midHeckeData N r S 𝒪 θ hc₁` be the resulting Hecke datum on $H^1(Nr,\top;\mathcal O)=\operatorname{Hom}(\Gamma_H(Nr),\mathcal O)$ with generators `Gen N r S`, operators `midOp` and residual characters $g\mapsto\theta(T_{\ell(g)})$. Let $h_1$ and $h_r$ witness [`CohCarrier.LevelLE N (N*r) ⊤ ⊤ d`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L330) for $d=1$ and $d=r$ (namely $N\mid Nr$, $d\mid (Nr)/N$, and compatibility of the unit subgroups). Then for every $\varphi\in H^1(Nr,\top;\mathcal O)$ annihilated by both degeneracy maps [`CohCarrier.jDeg`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L482) for $d=1$ and $d=r$ (each given by the $\Gamma$-transfer of the $d$-twisted pullback), the image of $\varphi$ under `toML`, the localisation map of $H^1(Nr,\top;\mathcal O)$ at the complement of the prime $\mathfrak m_\theta=\ker\tilde\theta\subseteq\mathcal O[X_g:g\in\text{Gen}]$, is zero.
--
--   This is the cohomological form of the failure of level raising at an auxiliary prime $r$ with $\operatorname{tr}\bar\rho(\mathrm{Frob}_r)^2\ne(r+1)^2$ (the converse half of Ribet's level-raising criterion): localised at the maximal ideal attached to $\theta$, no class at level $Nr$ is $r$-new. It is used to bound the rank of the localised cohomology at level $Nr$ by twice that at level $N$, in [`CuspForm.AuxLevel.finrank_midML_le_two_mul_finrank_baseML`](thm.html#CuspForm.AuxLevel.finrank_midML_le_two_mul_finrank_baseML).
